  "description": "ULETIQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H232 Dy6 N6 Ni8 O60,2(C2 H3 N1),4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3B (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni4B (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 25 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.024-4.050 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.53-132.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C120H232Dy6N6Ni8O60. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 16 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
